        "id": 1334530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-26T21:52:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, doing `memcpy` definitely helps reduce stack usage, following the call to `exercise_memset`. If we use a for loop, it would probably use a small enough stack footprint to not need any extra stack runway, but in a normal GNU/Linux GCC, this for loop should be replaced by a memcpy....so we may/may-not be back in the same scenario.",
      "parentUuid": "80f390fd_46a1a6e7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 68,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 68,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "c3bbbc0c9cd8811e2ae493acc2e5807a9a2bc37a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
