      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-26T22:21:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Confirmed that in a normal GNU/Linux GCC env, we don\u0027t use any of `space` when we invoke memcpy. We could discard it, but then we are assuming that anything that memcpy does will always fit within one minimal stack frame.",
      "parentUuid": "23671a32_e59f9082",
